---
id: AP-002
type: rule
family: guardrail-suppression
title: Rule-specific eslint-disable
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 2

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs]
allowlist: ['**/*.test.ts', '**/*.spec.ts', '**/__tests__/**', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: 'eslint-disable(?:-next-line|-line)?\s+[\w@/-]+'

related: [AP-001]
enabled: true
opt_in: true
---

Before disabling this rule, try to fix the code so it passes. If the
disable is genuinely necessary, add a comment explaining why this
specific case can't follow the rule.

A targeted disable is better than a blanket one, but the right
question is still: "why is this rule failing here, and can I fix the
code instead?"
